{"name":"Apple Sauce","hex":"#f4ebd2","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"apple sauce","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A culinary dish prepared by pureeing cooked apples.","Alternative spelling of applesauce (“nonsense”)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apple_sauce"}],"entries":[{"title":"Apple sauce","blocks":[{"text":"Apple sauce is a purée made of apples. It can be made with peeled or unpeeled apples and can be spiced or sweetened. Apple sauce is inexpensive and is widely consumed in North America and some parts of Europe."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Applesauce.jpg/330px-Applesauce.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple_sauce","wikidata":"Q618345"},{"title":"Apple","blocks":[{"text":"An apple is the round, edible fruit of an apple tree. Fruit trees of the orchard or domestic apple, the most widely grown in the genus, are cultivated worldwide. The tree originated in Central Asia, where its wild ancestor, Malus sieversii, is still found. Apples have been grown for thousands of years in Eurasia before they were introduced to the American continent by European colonists. Apples have cultural significance in many mythologies and religions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg/330px-Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple","wikidata":"Q89"},{"title":"Sauce","blocks":[{"text":"In cooking, a sauce is a liquid, cream, or semi-solid food, served on or used in preparing other foods. Most sauces are not normally consumed by themselves; they add flavour, texture, and visual appeal to a dish. Sauce is a French word probably from the post-classical Latin salsa, derived from the classical salsus 'salted'. Possibly the oldest recorded European sauce is garum, the fish sauce used by the Ancient Romans, while doubanjiang, the Chinese soy bean paste, is mentioned in Rites of Zhou 20."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/84/Lunch_sauces.jpg/330px-Lunch_sauces.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sauce","wikidata":"Q178359"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Homemade-applesauce-in-progress.png/500px-Homemade-applesauce-in-progress.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Homemade-applesauce-in-progress.png/1280px-Homemade-applesauce-in-progress.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Homemade-applesauce-in-progress.png/500px-Homemade-applesauce-in-progress.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Making apple sauce","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHomemade-applesauce-in-progress.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Latkas.jpg/500px-Latkas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Latkas.jpg/1280px-Latkas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Latkas.jpg/500px-Latkas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Latkes served with apple sauce and sour cream","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALatkas.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Malus_domestica_a1.jpg/500px-Malus_domestica_a1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thu